# I use cron to enforce my breaks & daily schedule ("horarium") as most of my
# work is being done on a PC and phone (I use an app to do sth. similar on my
# phone).

# Advantages as opposed to only using alarms:
#   1. I don't have to think about my schedule and manage the alarms.
#   2. Alarms can go unnoticed (e.g. if my phone is in a different room or out
#   of battery).
#   3. There is no postpone button. I don't waste my willpower to keep my
#   time-blocks sharp.
#   4. I don't have to think about turning off the PC and can just always
#   leave it on, when I go away.
#   5. It helps me to context switch between time blocks in my day (I use time
#   blocking), and keep my virtual desktops clean.
#   6. Breaks help me to reevaluate my priorities for the day (it sometimes
#   takes me up to 15 min to "unfocus" resp. mentally park the thing I was doing
#   before I am able to do focused prioritization).
#
#   Note: shutdown uses default "+1m" delay, hence if I am caught off guard, I
#   can return by turning my PC on back again and 1m is just enough time to
#   finish what I was doing.
#
# Disadvantages:
#   1. It is annoying during online calls - but this is also a blessing in
#   disguise as I am forced to stick online calls to my time-blocks, not the
#   other way around. However online calls need to be taken into consideration
#   when modifying the daily schedule.



*      0-6    * * *  root /usr/local/bin/notify_and_shutdown.sh "Sleep"

# --- 7 - 9 Time block 0 (phone off) ---

50-59   8      * * *  root /usr/local/bin/notify_and_shutdown.sh "Terce"

# --- 9 - 12 Time block 1 (phone off) ---

# --- Sext, lunch and walk (phone on) ---
*      12     * * *  root /usr/local/bin/notify_and_shutdown.sh "Lunch"

# --- 13 - 15 Time block 2 (phone off) ---

15-20/2 15     * * *  root /usr/bin/loginctl lock-sessions

# --- 15:30 - 17:40 Time block 3 (phone off) ---

# 17:40 - alarm on phone - supper

# --- 18:00 - 20:00 Bonus time block (optional, phone on)

*      20-23  * * *  root /usr/local/bin/notify_and_shutdown.sh "End of the day"


# === WEEKLY SCHEDULE ===
# Saturday - cleanup
*      17-20  * * Sat  root /sbin/shutdown
# Sunday - rest/sport
*      12-20  * * Sun  root /sbin/shutdown

